  "Windows are records; nothing is drawn, and ShowWindow is later work.",
  "Message 0x60, undocumented (wiert.me, 2020-12-22, lists it among loop messages without documentation), is posted to a system window of the thread some time after its window is activated: the probe met it after a posted WM_USER message on every run (wParam 0x80000001 on Server 2025, 1 on 2022), and the game dispatched one at seq 3491-3493 to a procedure it never saw. Its arrival varies (one execution met two in the WM_QUIT drain); w2m posts none, and the derivation takes it out of each drain (windows_rows).",
  "On Windows DefWindowProcW's WM_ACTIVATE sends WM_IME_SETCONTEXT, WM_IME_NOTIFY and the first WM_SETFOCUS from inside; w2m sends them from SetFocus in the same order. A procedure that keeps WM_ACTIVATE from DefWindowProcW would get them in w2m and not on Windows.",
  "LoadImageW of a cursor file left the last error 0 in the probe; the game's call left 6 (its file, written past the capture's 32-call count, is not on the record).",
  "Where CW_USEDEFAULT places a window depends on the windows the desktop made before (160 and 32 seen for the laptop probe's first, 26, 52, 78 and 130 on the runners); w2m's cascade starts at 32, steps by 32 and does not wrap (the first execution of each laptop run put its fourth default-placed window back at 32 after 224).",
  "The default height is fitted: 3/4 of the work area's height less 25 on the laptop at 120 DPI (740 on 1020), less 21 on both runners at 96."
